  ./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:12:claim_summary: "The v2 covariantly damped Maxwell-Debye layer is not perfectly matched."
  ./memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-v2-covariant-model-not-perfectly-matched.md:18:For a planar x-interface with constant layer coefficient rho_x=rho>0, rho_y=0, Laplace parameter Re s>0, and tangential Fourier number k_y, the physical Maxwell-Debye admittance is Y0^2=A(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2), where A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s).  The v2 covariantly damped model has Yrho^2=A_rho(s)/mu+k_y^2/(mu^2 s(s+rho)), where A_rho(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau(s+rho)).  Hence Yrho^2-Y0^2=-rho[chi tau/(mu(1+tau(s+rho))(1+tau s))+k_y^2/(mu^2 s^2(s+rho))], which is generically nonzero.  Therefore the interface reflection coefficient (Y0-Yrho)/(Y0+Yrho) is generically nonzero: the model is dissipative but not perfectly matched.  Full derivation: artifacts/proofs/stage3_v2_perfect_matching_test.md.
  ./ITERIS_INPUT_GUIDE.md:21:Analyze sources/energy_functional_problem.tex. The model is the displayed 2D Maxwell--PML system with P, P_{z,1}, P_{z,2}, Q_x, Q_y and PEC boundary condition. Start with the alpha = 1 case of P + tau^alpha partial_t^alpha P = chi E; do not remove P from the model. Search first for a monotone decreasing energy functional in two dimensions. If no monotone energy can be found, derive the strongest bounded-energy/no-abnormal-growth estimate possible, in the spirit of MPML long-time stability, or identify a verified obstruction for natural quadratic energies. Only after the alpha = 1 model is understood, examine whether the fractional case 0 < alpha < 1 can be added as a positive memory energy. Write the final result to results/energy_functional_report.md.
